{"availability":"available","full":"lumos-vis/Lumos","name":"Lumos","description":"Visualize your interaction traces during visual data analysis","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":3,"forks":6,"created":"2024-08-09T02:22:23Z","updated":"2026-09-16T02:28:40Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://lumos-1stu.onrender.com","topics":["analytic-provenance","bias","exploration-bias","interaction-traces","provenance","visual-analytics","visual-data-analysis","visualization","webapp"],"demo":"https://lumos-1stu.onrender.com/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:17.747Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:17.747Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:17.747Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T03:24:17.747Z","stars":3,"forks":6}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Lumos is a visual data analysis tool that captures and shows the interaction history with data to increase awareness of such analytic behaviors. Using in-situ (at the place of interaction) and ex-situ (in an external view) visualization techniques, Lumos provides real-time feedback to users for them to reflect on their activities. For example, Lumos highlights datapoints that have been previously examined in the same visualization (in-situ) and also overlays them on the underlying data distribution (i.e., baseline distribution) in a separate visualization (ex-situ).","This codebase comprises an easy-to-extend Angular frontend and a Python 3.10, SocketIO, AIOHTTP backend with an API for real-time bi-directional communication with the frontend over the HTTP REST and websocket protocols."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lumos-vis/Lumos/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c8022430085a5e65083fdc9a8818b9fe70196561f6fe7841fc8f26473f21ddbf","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:17.870Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:17.870Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Lumos is a visual data analysis tool t